WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.190
Here's an old legend, told as a puzzle.

2
00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:07.020
Put one grain of rice on the
first square of a chessboard.

3
00:00:07.070 --> 00:00:09.040
Two grains on square two.

4
00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:10.990
Four on square three.

5
00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:12.870
Eight on square four.

6
00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:15.540
Each square doubles the one before.

7
00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:17.630
The piles still look tiny.

8
00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:20.290
But a chessboard has sixty-four squares.

9
00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:23.400
So how many grains end
up on square sixty-four?

10
00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:24.750
Double sixty-four?

11
00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:26.190
Sixty-four squared?

12
00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:28.000
Or something else?

13
00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:30.950
In this mission, you'll
meet two kinds of rule.

14
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:35.240
A term-to-term rule, like double,
and a position-to-term rule,

15
00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:36.640
the nth term.

16
00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:40.620
You'll see that a linear sequence
adds the same amount each time.

17
00:00:40.670 --> 00:00:44.820
And a geometric sequence multiplies
by the same number each time.

18
00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:48.770
Your mission: find how many
grains are on square sixty-four.
